Maintainer decision 2026-11-03: mcp-hub becomes the second consumer of the bundle's planned binary release form (`binary = mcp-hub` in dist.ini, action `dzil-binary@v1`, shared install.sh/install.ps1) — see the draft ~/dev/p5-mcp-wiki/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-03-binary-release-design.md and the spike ~/dev/mcp-wiki-binary-spike. This card therefore covers only the per-dist part: the -M list for everything loaded by name, local pp build + verify, the no-Perl smoke, the EV decision, the README section. No own release-binaries.yml and no install.sh in this repo; those come from the bundle (its board, k17 and successors). mcp-hub's requirements on dzil-binary@v1 go to the bundle board once the worker reports.

From k29 research (verified on the scratchpad binary): the packed hub strips PERL5LIB/PERLLIB/PERL5OPT/PERLIO — for itself AND for its stdio children. A local::lib-installed Perl stdio server (e.g. cpanm'd mcp-wiki) started by the packed hub dies with 'Can't locate …'. Workaround: `"env": {"PERL5LIB": "${HOME}/perl5/lib/perl5"}` on the entry; `${PERL5LIB}` is a config error there because it is already gone at config load. The README binary section must say this. Whether the hub should restore the caller's PERL5LIB for children instead is a lib/ question — note it for mcp-hub-worker if you think so.

