2026-11-03 18:33 Notes for mcp-hub-worker (nothing in lib/ or bin/ was changed):
(1) bin/mcp-hub takes -c anywhere in argv as --config, so 'mcp-hub get -c JSON URL' breaks: Mojolicious get's -c ends up read as a config path. --content works.
(2) An https url upstream without IO::Socket::SSL logs 'handshake failed: IO::Socket::SSL 2.009+ required' but answers agents 'upstream not ready yet' (the 503 meaning) forever, instead of failing. The same happens in a CPAN minimal install and in the Docker image: neither cpanfile nor Dockerfile carries IO::Socket::SSL.
(3) 'mcp-hub status' exits 0 when the hub is down. This is documented, but scripts cannot detect it.
(4) The help listing offers Mojolicious' prefork command, which goes against the 'never prefork' hazard.
(5) Windows is blocked by Upstream::Stdio and MCP::Hub::Docker (fork + socketpair(AF_UNIX) + pipe streamed through Mojo::IOLoop; select on Windows polls sockets only), by the SIGHUP reload, and by HOME/XDG paths. ClaudeSessions is Linux-only (handled).
For the bundle board (dzil-binary):
(a) The -M set: 30 modules are invisible to pp's scanner (MCP::Hub::Command::*, MCP::Hub::Native::*, Mojolicious::Command::*/Plugin::*, Mojo::Server::*, YAML::PP::Schema::Core). Best taken from 'perl -Ilib scripts/loaded-modules.pl' rather than a static dist.ini list.
